      "head_commit": {
        "id": "94c5e3e6c2cc2c56717e938d47449c9c4d61f051",
        "tree_id": "121c9cd64143dc3b33a0c58bd9d2b7331c5dac6f",
        "message": "Fix mmlu zero-shot evaluation in DeepEP DeepSeek-V2 tests\n\ntest_mmlu scored 0.000 across all categories in run 37776934235 -- its\nfirst-ever real execution (previously masked by the CI failfast because\ntest_gsm8k always failed first).\n\nRoot cause (matches the Aug 12 ticket on the same symptom, whose fix was\nnever synced to these cases): num_shots=5 makes MMLUEval prepend five\nfew-shot examples rendered by format_multichoice_question_example, which\nis the QUERY template WITHOUT the answer -- the model receives six\nconsecutive unanswered questions, its completion-style continuation does\nnot follow the \"Answer: $LETTER\" contract, and the answer regex fails\nsystematically (random guessing would score ~0.25, so 0.0 means\nextraction failure, not model failure).\n\nApply the Aug 12 fix to both cases:\n\n- drop num_shots=5 from the eval args (0-shot single-question template)\n- expect_score 0.58 -> 0.38 (baseline re-measured on GPU per the ticket;\n  NPU measured higher)\n\nAlso bump est_time 600 -> 1200 now that the file runs the full gsm8k set\nplus a real mmlu eval (~11 min measured per case in run 37776934235).\n\nsingle-test-npu.yml (verification-only, kept until the CI result is\nreviewed): re-apply the round-2 adaptations (a3-8 runner, B081 image,\nin-shell export GITHUB_EVENT_NAME=workflow_dispatch) and run both cases\nin full (test_gsm8k + test_mmlu), no test-method scoping this round.",
